// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6168 add sigma rules for Windows Sandbox
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6168
// Pull request author: unrooted
// Change: new rule
// Title: Headless SYSTEM-Context Command Execution Via Windows Sandbox CLI
// Sigma ID: 86fdab07-ef1e-4528-bf4b-e1f9eefd1546
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Konrad 'unrooted' Klawikowski
// Date: 2026-07-22 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, privilege-escalation, T1218, T1564.006
// Description: Detects use of the wsb.exe exec subcommand with -r System, which executes a command inside an
//   already-running Windows Sandbox in the NT AUTHORITY\SYSTEM context.
// False positives:
//   - Internal IT or development automation that scripts SYSTEM-context tasks inside sandboxes for testing
//   - Sandbox-based CI runners that need elevated execution
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/windows/security/application-security/application-isolation/windows-sandbox/windows-sandbox-cli#exec
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/OtherMSBinaries/Wsb/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/e690cf7a8be81d20e2688ad8cc3866640f1d8fce/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_wsb_exec_system.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\wsb.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "wsb.exe") and ProcessCommandLine contains " exec " and (ProcessCommandLine contains " -r System" or ProcessCommandLine contains " --run-as System")
